  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/rhinogobius-zhoui-2/",
      "html": "<p>This freshwater goby, which attains a maximum length of 4-5 cm, is one of the most attractive discoveries of ornamental fish of the last years. In the beginning the fish were extremely expensive, but they are now available at a comparably moderate price.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/rhinogobius-zhoui-2/",
      "html": "<p>Rhinogobius zhoui originates from China.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/rhinogobius-zhoui-2/",
      "html": "<p>In the natural habitat, brooks, it lives along with the well known goby Rhinogobius duospilus (often better known under the synonymous name R. wui) and other species. R. zhoui is a pure freshwater goby.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/rhinogobius-zhoui-2/",
      "html": "<p>Keeping and feeding the fish is otherwise unproblematical.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/rhinogobius-zhoui-2/",
      "html": "<p>Due to the subtropical region the fish come from, keep them in unheated aquaria (16-22°C). The water should be clean and have some current.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/rhinogobius-zhoui-2/",
      "html": "<p>The small fish change their coloration quite often and quickly. It is a lot of fun to observe an aquarium containing these tiny gobies, which are always in the mood for a harmless quarrel.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/rhinogobius-zhoui-2/",
      "html": "<p>Males are distinguished from the females by the broad white seams in the fins and the more intensive colours.</p>"
    }
  ],
